        "original_id": "a3162fad-fb9b-5b86-97d2-4c2fdd73d760",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: My Darkest Days, Human Drama\n- People: Matt Walst, Brendan McMillan, Doug Oliver, Reid Henry, Johnny Indovina\n- Places: Peterborough, Ontario\n- Songs: \"Casual Sex\"\n\nFacts:\n- Human Drama is an American alternative rock band formed in 1985 and led by singer-songwriter Johnny Indovina.\n- Human Drama released six studio albums before splitting in 2005, with Johnny Indovina as its only constant member.\n- My Darkest Days were a Canadian rock band based in Peterborough, Ontario.\n- My Darkest Days consisted of lead singer Matt Walst, bassist Brendan McMillan, drummer Doug Oliver, and keyboardist Reid Henry.\n- \"Casual Sex\" is a song by the Canadian rock band My Darkest Days.",
